; Block npm lifecycle scripts (preinstall / install / postinstall) repo-wide.
;
; No bus tool call is ever gated on a human: production turns run
; permissionMode 'default' with a canUseTool callback that auto-approves
; everything except AskUserQuestion. (Both routers wire the ask-gate hook,
; so the bypassPermissions branch in runner.ts is reached only by callers
; that skip it — i.e. tests. See the note in server/src/bus/guardrail.ts.)
; Auto-approve-everything is bypass in effect, so a malicious transitive
; postinstall script still lands as direct RCE on an operator's machine.
; The legitimate native build (better-sqlite3) is re-enabled explicitly via
; `npm rebuild better-sqlite3 --foreground-scripts` in CI and dev setup.
ignore-scripts=true

; Supply-chain hardening: refuse to resolve any version published < 7 days ago.
; A freshly-published (possibly account-takeover / malicious) release must age
; a week before npm will install it — the window in which most poisoned
; publishes are caught and yanked. `npm ci` installs the lockfile verbatim, so
; this only gates fresh *resolution* (`npm install`, transitive bumps); it pairs
; with the dependabot `cooldown` in .github/dependabot.yml.
min-release-age=7
